# {{SYSTEM}} — the specification

**Scaffolded {{DATE}} by `kit spec new {{SYSTEM_ID}}`.** This folder holds one specification,
written to the standards of the method: `SDD-01`, and the standard the table below names for each
slot. Each slot's checklist and template are produced by its standard's build and stand in the
delivery kit, under `templates/spec/checklists/` and `templates/spec/artefacts/`; `kit slot <n>`
names both.

## How it is laid out

**One folder per thing `SDD-01` §4 names**, numbered in the order they come into existence.
Each carries a `README.md` saying what it is, who writes it, what governs it, when it is
written, and what a person working in it has to know.

{{SLOT_TABLE}}

Beside them: `_conformance/` the rule-by-rule claims · `_amendments/` what use teaches the
standards · `_findings/` gaps with owners · `_rulings/` what the owner decided · `_sessions/`
commissions and reports · `_machinery/` plans, renderers and checks · `_reviews/` generated
pages for a person.

**An empty slot is information.** It says the thing does not exist yet. No slot is ever
filled to make the tree look finished.

## The order the slots are written in

`SDD-01` §5. Four things are settled **once for the whole system** — 00, 01, 02 at naming
level, 03. The rest of the shared groundwork (05) sits below them. Three things are **walked
again for every goal** — 06, 07, 08. The entity model (02) is **deepened to structural level
as the goals demand it**. The architecture specification (04) runs **alongside, to the end**.
All three per-goal things enter **the review** together. Then **the interaction design (08a)**
reads the accepted screens of every goal the application model will carry, and the owner
accepts it; and only then 09, which names it by its path and checksum, then 10.

**A ratchet, not a one-way march: any step may be entered again, but only from above.**

