## What this folder is for

The specification is the visible output. **It is not the point.** The point is
`_amendments/` — the list of places where a standard could not be followed, was ambiguous,
cost more than it was worth, or turned out to be silent, each recorded with the moment it
happened. That list is what amends the set; the specification is what proves the list was
earned.

`SDD-01` §16 states the condition this folder exists to change: *no document produced so far
carries a conformance claim made rule by rule.*

## The rules this folder is under

- **What software generated is never edited by hand.** A correction goes into the source.
- **A correction lands in the document that owns the fact**, never where it was noticed.
- **A gap is a finding with an owner, never a local invention.** The most important rule of
  all when an assistant is doing the writing.
- **A claim that something follows a standard is made rule by rule, or it is not a claim.**
- **Gaps stay open and counted.** Never signed off to turn a light green. A refusal is
  answered, not worked around.
- **Where the work stands is read from the work, never remembered.**
- **`00_customer_documents/` is never edited, for any reason.**

